.TH SPINCLASS-LOCAL-DEFAULT-REF 7 "" "spinclass" "Spinclass Reference"
.SH NAME
spinclass-local-default-ref \- why a merge may leave the local default branch behind
.SH DESCRIPTION
A merge targets the default
.I remote's
default branch (e.g.\&
.BR origin/master ).
It rebases onto it, gates against it, and lands by pushing to it.
Session creation cuts new branches from the same ref.
.PP
The root checkout's
.I local
default branch is never read for correctness.
After the landing push, spinclass fast-forwards it to the landed commit as a
convenience \(em using git's own
.B merge \-\-ff\-only
semantics \(em and reports the result as an
.B advance local <branch>
step.
.PP
A local-only merge
.RB ( local_only )
is the exception: its remote is the checkout itself, so there the
fast-forward of the local branch IS the landing, and a refusal fails the merge.
.SH WHY A SKIP IS FINE
When the fast-forward is not possible, the step is reported as
.B # SKIP
and the merge still succeeds.
The operation that matters \(em the commit landing on the remote \(em has already
happened; failing it retroactively over a convenience ref would misreport what
occurred.
Spinclass's own checks (close, clean, auto-close) already count a branch as
integrated when either the local default branch or its remote-tracking ref
contains it.
.PP
If you read the local default branch to decide whether work merged, read
.B <remote>/<branch>
instead.
.SH RECONCILING
The skip reason names the cause and the command:
.TP
.B uncommitted changes
Your edits in the checkout overlap the incoming change.
Commit or stash them, then run
.BR "git merge \-\-ff\-only origin/<branch>" .
.TP
.B diverged
The local branch has commits the remote lacks and vice versa.
Rebase it onto, or reset it to,
.BR origin/<branch> ;
which one is your call.
.TP
.B ahead
The local branch has commits the remote lacks.
Push them, or drop them.
.SH METRICS
Each remote landing sends statsd counters to stats-me
.RB ( stats\-me\-clients (7)):
.BR spinclass.merge.landed ,
.BR spinclass.merge.push_refused ,
.BR spinclass.merge.local_advance.ok ,
.B spinclass.merge.local_advance.skip
and
.BR spinclass.merge.local_advance.skip_reason. { dirty_overlap , diverged , ahead , error }.
.B ok
plus
.B skip
always equals
.BR landed .
Nothing is sent unless
.B STATSD_HOST
or
.B STATSD_PORT
is set;
.B SPINCLASS_DISABLE_STATSD=1
turns emission off.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spinclass-merge-this-session (1),
.BR spinclass-merge (1),
.BR spinclass-start (1)
.PP
spinclass FDR 0029 (detached landing worktree), spinclass#295, spinclass#315.
